## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of cross-service idempotency in a CNPA stack, covering HTTP, DB, Kafka, and lake sinks.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys across HTTP, DB, and Kafka
- Transactional writes and idempotent producers
- Deduplication in data lake sinks
- End-to-end validation under retries

## Code Example

```sql
CREATE TABLE idempotency_keys (
  key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now(),
  result JSONB
);
```

```java
@PostMapping("/update")
public Response update(@RequestHeader("Idempotency-Key") String key, @RequestBody Event e) {
  if (idempotency.exists(key)) return idempotency.getResult(key);
  // begin tx
  updateUser(e);
  kafkaProducer.send(...);
  idempotency.save(key, newResult);
  return ok;
}
```

